  "summary": "Add a backend-owned priority-only queue export and a fail-closed Run Once launch scope that reuses normal pipeline processing policy.",
  "reason": "Operators can mark queue rows as high priority, but priority currently changes ordering only and offers no safe way to run just a few queued files.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "local-api",
    "pipeline-engine",
    "queue-launch",
    "state-artifacts",
    "webview"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "Queue priority affects ordering, while Backend Queue Run Once still accepts the full authoritative queue snapshot.",
  "behavior_after": "Queue can create a backend-owned export of runnable effective-high entries, and Launch can run exactly that exported membership through normal Run Once processing with runtime fingerprint revalidation.",
